# Codex-side agent credentials. Copy to `.env.codex`, which is gitignored.
#
# Board row 4601. These two logins are the ONLY database access a Codex agent has. Each reaches
# one table on one project and nothing else, proven by refusal tests on board row 4603 rather
# than by reading the grant table.
#
# The passwords are not in this repository and never go on the board. Ric has them.
#
# The host is the POOLER host, which is not the same as `db.<ref>.supabase.co`. Read it from the
# Supabase dashboard for that project, under Connect, and keep the port it gives you. Do not
# guess the `aws-0` / `aws-1` prefix: both resolve, only one is yours.

RAAYDR_BOARD_URL=postgresql://codex_board.kpfcxakyhtxjwmcbxndc:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres
RAAYDR_TRACKER_URL=postgresql://codex_tracker.kfgootvqcdnfdzzustyb:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres

# ============================================================================
# A CODEX AGENT NEEDS NEITHER OF THE ABOVE. It uses HTTPS.
# ============================================================================
#
# Set these as PLAIN environment variables in the Codex environment, not as Codex "secrets":
# secrets are stripped before the agent phase, so a secret would not be there to read.
#
#   RAAYDR_BOARD_ENDPOINT=https://kpfcxakyhtxjwmcbxndc.supabase.co/functions/v1/board
#   RAAYDR_BOARD_TOKEN=<token from Ric>
#
# RAAYDR_BOARD_TOKEN is OPTIONAL. If Codex injects an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header at
# its proxy for that host, leave it unset and the agent never holds the token at all.
#
# Allowlist exactly one host: kpfcxakyhtxjwmcbxndc.supabase.co
